title: "HackMatch — US-034: Unread Loading and Mark-Read Sequence"
---
%%{init: {"theme":"base","themeVariables":{"background":"#ffffff","primaryColor":"#e8f1ff","primaryTextColor":"#1f2937","primaryBorderColor":"#3b82f6","lineColor":"#4b5563","secondaryColor":"#f1e8ff","tertiaryColor":"#fff7d6","fontFamily":"Arial, sans-serif"},"sequence":{"useMaxWidth":true,"diagramMarginX":25,"diagramMarginY":18,"actorMargin":34,"width":165,"height":60,"boxMargin":8,"messageMargin":24,"noteMargin":10}}}%%
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Part as Active verified PART
    participant UI as Chat, team chat, or DM view
    participant Provider as ChatUnreadProvider
    participant API as Chat API
    participant Service as Read and unread services
    participant DB as PostgreSQL RPCs

    Part->>UI: Enter authenticated application
    UI->>Provider: Start session-scoped unread state
    Provider->>API: GET /api/chat/unread-counts
    API->>API: Require authenticated active PART
    API->>Service: Get participant activity summary
    Service->>DB: get_participant_chat_activity_counts
    DB->>DB: Authorize channels, team membership, and DM pair
    DB->>DB: Count messages and mentions after each cursor
    DB-->>Service: Count-only authorized rows
    Service-->>Provider: Per-conversation and aggregate counts
    Provider-->>UI: Render channel, DM, navigation, and mention badges

    Part->>UI: Open a conversation
    UI->>API: Load authorized messages
    API-->>UI: Ordered safe messages
    UI->>Provider: Mark latest visible message read
    Provider->>API: POST /api/chat/read
    API->>Service: Authorize conversation before storage
    Service->>DB: mark_chat_conversation_read
    DB->>DB: Monotonic tuple upsert and fresh count query
    DB-->>Service: Cursor, advanced flag, unread counts
    Service-->>Provider: Server-confirmed safe result
    Provider-->>UI: Update affected badges and reconcile summary

    alt Mark-read fails or access changes
        API-->>Provider: Safe denied or unavailable error
        Provider-->>UI: Keep confirmed badges and show recovery state
    end

    Note over Provider,DB: PostgreSQL cursors remain authoritative across refresh.<br/>Changing sessions discards the previous participant cache.

